==Strategy==
This stage is initially daunting due to The Perfect Cyclone's massive 650 standing range, as its rapid, ceaseless LD attacks reach all the way down to 250. Despite having a sizable blindspot and somewhat low DPS for a cyclone, most units simply could not withstand its onslaught long enough to get within range. Fortunately, the peons covering it don't put up much of a fight, and the stage basically plays itself if enough units slip in.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako/Octopus Cat]] - One of the best units to use on this stage, Sadako is a disposable [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] tanker specialist. With its low range, Resistance and 30% chance to Weaken Floating enemies to 50%, it has no difficulty creeping inside the blindspot and taking it from there, potentially enabling other units to proceed inside if its Weaken ability activates so they could fight off the Doge Darks. If you don't have Octopus's [[Talents]], use Sadako as it has a faster attack rate.
*[[Mummy Sumo (Super Rare Cat)|Mama Mummy Sumo]] - Arguably superior to Kotatsu from certain perspectives, Mama Mummy Sumo targets Black in addition to Floating and is Immune to Knockback, so Trolly Bloggers cannot hope to displace her.
*[[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera]]/[[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Titan]]/[[Brainwashed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Titan]] - Strong but expensive melee units that can, with some assistance, walk inside The Perfect Cyclone's blindspot and provide support. Their health won't stand up to The Perfect Cyclone's attacks, so they'll require a bit of assistance themselves, although their singular knockback are helpful in this regard.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Bulky Melee [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]]/Tanker - They'll rush up into The Perfect Cyclone's blindspot and effectively crush it with ease. Also, with their HP, they'll be able to withstand a few hits from the Doge Darks while dealing damage to kill them, though be wary of the Trolly Bloggers and Doge Darks.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]] - The greatest choice out of all the melee Ubers, as not only does she have the standard melee Uber capabilities, but also resistance to Floating and knockback immunity, effectively being the '''perfect''' unit for this stage.
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]] - An effective damage dealer and crowd-controller for the cyclone, as they wield a guaranteed Level 3 [[Wave Attack]] and a 30% chance to [[Knockback]] the Cyclone, but is vulnerable to Trolly Blogger, as a stack of these can prevent this unit from attacking at all.
*[[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rusher-class]] Ubers - They can blitz to Perfect Cyclone's blindspot like bulky melee ubers, but it's harder to get them to shine on here, as you'll need to be aware of the peons, and also some of them could just end up getting knocked back and dying before even getting to the blindspot. If you're going with one of these, make sure to have Sadako, as his weaken can make this much less likely to happen.
*[[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Balalan Pasalan]] - Very effective on this stage, especially in [[True Form]]. It can freeze the boss, allowing more time for cats to get in its blind spot. Piccolan Pasalan's 6-second weaken makes it a lot easier for other cats to get there, to the point where even [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank]] can manage to squeeze its way in.
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]] - He is one of the few ubers that can deal huge damage to The Perfect Cyclone while remaining far enough to be safe from its strikes, without having to enter its blind spot. Beware of the peons especially when using him, as Lufalan Pasalan is a single-target attacker.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]] - Just like Lufalan Pasalan, he can snipe Perfect Cyclone from a far distance. Although doesn't provide as much damage as the choice above, he can destroy the peons as well thanks to his Area Attack. At good levels he may even surpass Lufalan in helpfulness due to his knockback against Floating enemies.

